{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485580-2e-blood-sorcery-and-mage-the-awakening","id":485580,"title":"2E Blood Sorcery and Mage: The Awakening","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-19T12:46:13-07:00","id":485580,"title":"2E Blood Sorcery and Mage: The Awakening","content":"So, for those of you that have the 1E Blood Sorcery book, I'm sure you recognize a lot of elements from Mage: The Awakening's Sorcery in the 1st Edition.<br /> <br /> For the 2E of Mage, they've updated and streamlined a lot about the Magic System to make it a little less funky with numbers, like doing away with extended action sorcery and raw success pools.<br /> <br /> If you were going to update Blood Sorcery to the 2nd Edition, with its ritual factors et al., would you consider altering the system for adjudicating Spell Factors? Or keep it as it is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T13:00:33-07:00","id":485601,"title":"","content":"I personally don't use Themes, but I have to ask - is Mage out? Isn't it a bit premature to ask without the full book or rules? Or are the full rules somewhere? I've gneerally kept up with mage, and while it seems that the rules are stream lined, I don't think we have everything...<br /> <br /> Maybe including links to the updated rules would be helpful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-19-2015, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T13:23:03-07:00","id":485609,"title":"","content":"The <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/a-lever-and-a-firm-place-to-stand/\" target=\"_blank\">Yantras</a> blog is where they defined that it now works like that, a single roll with spell factors as penalties and the like.<br /> <br /> It is a bit premature, fair enough. I was interested in homebrewing something using the Blood Sorcery presented in <i>Blasphemies </i>as a base, and was wondering if I should try to come up with an alternative way to do Spell Factors based on what we know of Mage, since the new system sounds a bit nicer for sorcerous types.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, it might be more appropriate for this thread to go to Mage's subforum, mea culpa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T14:45:13-07:00","id":485734,"title":"","content":"I can move the thread to the Mage subforum if you like, but I think it's equally appropriate here or there.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like that Supernal Magic and Blood Sorcery use (or will use) different systems. Helps differentiate the them a bit more, you know? The Themes and factors could use revisiting though, in light of some of the new rituals previewed from Secrets of the Covenants. I can't imagine how Apple of Eden could possibly be made using only one dot of Themes and for additional successes for Factors, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T15:00:08-07:00","id":485746,"title":"","content":"I think one important aspect of Blood Sorcery using Extended Actions is the fact that the target of hostile Sorcery gets a chance to intervene. If it was a single Instant roll then this would either mean the victim would always have a specific set time to react which would never change, no matter how well the sorcerer prepares (to get the required successes faster) or does not even get the chance to counteract (if the sympathy to the sorcerer only kicks in at the moment the spell goes off). As such, Extended Actions work well to keep that aspect in.<br /> <br /> That being said, I like that they are moving away from using Potency with the new rituals and instead simply use flat numbers or the sorcerer's dots in the Sorcery Discipline. With Potency straight from the 2e Core, rituals were wildly unpredictable. Depending on your luck with the dice (which meant not just your overall successes, but also *when* you rolled them) rituals could have been extremely powerful (instant-torpor Touch of the Morrigan, for example) or really weak. You always wanted to roll as close to succeeding on the second-to-last roll without actually crossing the threshold and then roll a lot of successes on the last roll. That was a really awkward system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T02:08:38-07:00","id":486151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485580-2e-blood-sorcery-and-mage-the-awakening?p=485746#post485746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one important aspect of Blood Sorcery using Extended Actions is the fact that the target of hostile Sorcery gets a chance to intervene. If it was a single Instant roll then this would either mean the victim would always have a specific set time to react which would never change, no matter how well the sorcerer prepares (to get the required successes faster) or does not even get the chance to counteract (if the sympathy to the sorcerer only kicks in at the moment the spell goes off). As such, Extended Actions work well to keep that aspect in.<br /> <br /> That being said, I like that they are moving away from using Potency with the new rituals and instead simply use flat numbers or the sorcerer's dots in the Sorcery Discipline. With Potency straight from the 2e Core, rituals were wildly unpredictable. Depending on your luck with the dice (which meant not just your overall successes, but also *when* you rolled them) rituals could have been extremely powerful (instant-torpor Touch of the Morrigan, for example) or really weak. You always wanted to roll as close to succeeding on the second-to-last roll without actually crossing the threshold and then roll a lot of successes on the last roll. That was a really awkward system.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But... that's not how it works. If you want your powerful spell, you set your Target Successes higher, for as much as you want, and then anything you roll above that is just a bonus you didn't need (but it helps)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T03:09:16-07:00","id":486181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485580-2e-blood-sorcery-and-mage-the-awakening?p=486151#post486151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But... that's not how it works. If you want your powerful spell, you set your Target Successes higher, for as much as you want, and then anything you roll above that is just a bonus you didn't need (but it helps)</div> </div> </div> </div>If you use the Blood Sorcery supplement, yes. But the rules from the 2e Core do not have that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T03:32:31-07:00","id":486185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485580-2e-blood-sorcery-and-mage-the-awakening?p=486181#post486181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you use the Blood Sorcery supplement, yes. But the rules from the 2e Core do not have that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah alright. Well in my opinion 2e Core really did little in the name of the sorcery, precisely because of the Blood Sorcery supplement. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T03:35:53-07:00","id":486187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485580-2e-blood-sorcery-and-mage-the-awakening?p=486185#post486185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah alright. Well in my opinion 2e Core really did little in the name of the sorcery, precisely because of the Blood Sorcery supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, which is why I like the new rituals from Secrets of the Covenants. They are much better for the basic 2e system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T03:38:54-07:00","id":486190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485580-2e-blood-sorcery-and-mage-the-awakening?p=486187#post486187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, which is why I like the new rituals from Secrets of the Covenants. They are much better for the basic 2e system.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I do hope that their Theme equivalents are going to happen as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T06:52:18-07:00","id":486296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485580-2e-blood-sorcery-and-mage-the-awakening?p=485609#post485609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/a-lever-and-a-firm-place-to-stand/\" target=\"_blank\">Yantras</a> blog is where they defined that it now works like that, a single roll with spell factors as penalties and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not really sure if its applicable. Most spells, in 1e Mage, are single action, with ritual spells being something that changes single action spells into long term extended action. This 1e system is what the themes, and the current Target Numbers in 2e Requiem, are based off of.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if these rolls have target number of success requirements or not, however. Are we going back to one success to execute the entire thing for most spells? Well, that wouldn't work for combat or healing magic, I don't think. This is the part where I'm stalled on any kind of conversion.<br /> <br /> As for specific Instruments, and things like Demesne? We have several merits that add into magic. Library, the altar merit, etc. These become +1 factors instead of +1 dice each. So, that part is easy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Admittedly, it might be more appropriate for this thread to go to Mage's subforum, mea culpa. </div> </div> </div>The only thing I'd go into Mage for is a more accurate idea of what mages do to cast spells in 2e from the scattered things. There might have been more hints dropped in a thread by Dave, or something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/485580-2e-blood-sorcery-and-mage-the-awakening?p=486190#post486190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I do hope that their Theme equivalents are going to happen as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> Doubtful. Themes are not the core book way of doing magic, and I bet most writers are going to be using the default method. Yes, I know that there is a side bar, but that bar is an optional rule. Requiem 2e is a new core book, and we all know how the model is not needing anything beyond the core book. At best, we might hope for a web update, but I wouldn't hold my breath. Its not like the Themes don't come with their own system of improvising spells, so it should be easy to figure out the levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-20-2015, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}